# ek-courseedit: enter the 64DD COURSE EDIT mode from the SELECT MODE grid.
#
# EXPANSION-KIT-ONLY, AND DISK-ONLY. main_menu.c:222's EK arm bounces the cursor off
# MODE_COURSE_EDIT (4) and MODE_CREATE_MACHINE (7) whenever gLeoDriveConnectionState == 0, so
# on a no-disk build this replay walks to slot 5 (PRACTICE) instead and proves nothing. It is
# therefore NOT a corpus replay and is not in covdrift.sh's set: it is the B11d receipt, and
# it is only meaningful against a mounted 64DD image ([debug] disk_stream=2 + a .ndd under
# media/). Run it BOTH ways -- the no-disk run is the control that shows the bounce.
#
# Grid geometry (main_menu.c:612): index = (row * 4) + column, cursor starts at
# MODE_GP_RACE = 0 (game/common.c:21). One DOWN moves +4 -> MODE_COURSE_EDIT. A enters
# (main_menu.c:279 returns GAMEMODE_COURSE_EDIT = 0xD).
#
# SHOTs are hand-placed here rather than derived, because the thing being proved is "a
# specific screen exists at all", not "the schedule covers a census". See
# docs/research/native/ekdrive-progress.md.
build native/ekdrive
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=1 bridgemain=1 det=1
note SELECT MODE grid is 4x2; the EK arm bounces idx4/idx7 only when the drive is absent.
at 350
wait 1
at 400
press START 15 0
at 600
wait 1
shot menu_before
at 660
press DOWN 12 0
at 760
wait 1
shot menu_cursor
at 820
press A 12 0
at 1000
wait 1
shot enter_0
at 1200
wait 1
shot enter_1
at 1500
wait 1
shot enter_2
at 1900
wait 1
shot enter_3
at 2400
wait 1
shot enter_4
at 2900
wait 1
shot enter_5
len 3000
